==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|mis-|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|mis-||mis-|lang=ang}}, from Proto-Germanic {{recons|missa-||wrongly, badly|lang=gem-pro}}, related to {{term|miss|lang=en}}. In words borrowed from French, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|mes-|lang=fro}} (Modern {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|mé-|lang=fr}}), from {{etyl|frk|en}} {{recons|mis-|lang=frk}}, from Proto-Germanic {{recons|missa-||wrongly, badly|lang=gem-pro}}.

===Prefix===
{{en-prefix}}

# [[bad]], [[badly]], [[wrong]], [[wrongly]]
# [[lack]] or [[failure]]

====Derived terms====
*See [[:Category:English words prefixed with mis-]]

====See also====
* [[mal-]]
* [[miso-]]

